summary:
The swift port stands at its last commit (sdkgen 55675fd5, tools 0fa653a). Every number I re-ran matches the fixer's report:
- build exit 0 with the tree clean;
- guard and reader 5/5;
- guard account: derived 45, cited 13, language 1, convention 5;
- golden 2/2;
- SCRATCH=1 REGEN=1 fails as expected (OPEN 26/3/95, blocks 35/28/13, UNATTESTED 1 `named`, less often 1);
- REGEN=1 passes with exit 0 (same ledger and blocks table);
- suite without lanes: 2601 tests, 2596 pass, 0 fail, 5 skipped.

Files touched: all 7 changed sdkgen files are swift's own or the golden, and the tools commits touch only swift files. Outside swift, only the Swift blocks of the 19 root READMEs differ from base32. The fix changed no generated byte: my out/new is identical to the reviewer's pre-fix out/new (0 files differ).

What I checked against the runtime:
- R1, matchv copy: the fact is now true and cited. The sentence still does not print it, because ReadmeRef.ts memberText 'matchArg' ignores copy. It is correctly recorded as an additive shared change: only swift declares copy on a match member.
- R2, body values: the fact now names `.nat`, matching Value.swift:87. It is printed in 0 variations.
- R3, printers: they now build from facts.unwrap and facts.record.
- R4/R6, record expression: the fixer's whole-record check in swift's forms is weaker than reported. My fresh attack set facts.record to `({var}.asNative)?.data()`, which drops the cast and would not compile. The guard passed 5/5, because the check only asks that the captured unwrap be a word-bounded substring of the runtime quote, and `asNative` is one. It was caught only by hand records: tutorial OPEN 5, reference 1, blocks 3.
- Second fresh attack: the call printer dropped `, nil`, giving `load(nil)` against a two-parameter op with no defaults. The guard passed. Normal mode caught it through blocks OPEN 10/10/10 against OLD blocks. In SCRATCH mode it showed only as more block classes for a person to read: reference 13 to 19, tutorial 35 to 38.

Two things keep `ok` false:
1. The record check the fixer claimed whole is incomplete. It is fixable in swift's own forms file.
2. Three commits (sdkgen 824c5d41 and 55675fd5, tools 0fa653a) carry Co-Authored-By and Session lines that name a model. The brief and guide section 10 forbid that. The fixer flagged it but left it.

No Swift compiler is on the PATH, so 172 changed blocks (47 tutorial, 19 root, 106 reference) are compiled by nothing.
